$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Nozaki-Hiyama-Kishi Reaction, Typical
Experiment The solution of halogen derivative (0.15mmol), aldehyde
(0.2mmol), and NiCl2 (1mg) in 1mL DMA-THF 10:1 was degassed and treated
with the eluate (2.7mL) obtained as described previously (row 4, Table
1). Progress of the reaction was monitored with gas chromatography-mass
spectrometry (GC-MS) or ultra performance liquid chromatography-mass
spectrometry (UPLC-MS). After stirring at 50°C for the time given in
Table 2, the green reaction mixture was diluted with water (20mL) and
allowed to crystallize at rt (compounds 2a-2g), or extracted with ether
(3×50mL); the organic layer washed with brine (6×20mL) and dried with
magnesium sulfate. The crystalline material resulting after evaporation
was recrystallized from ethanol (compounds 1a, 1b). The isolated yields
and CrCl2 amounts are given in Table 2. Diphenylmethanol (1a) The title
compound was made from iodobenzene (30.6 mg) and benzaldehyde (21.2 mg).
Phenyl(p-tolyl)methanol (1b) The title compound was made from iodobenzene
(30.6 mg) and p-tolualdehyde (24.0 mg), or from 4-iodotoluene (32.7 mg)
and benzaldehyde (24.0 mg), resp. White solid, 26.9 mg and 26.7 mg, resp.
M.p. 53.2-54.2 °C (ref.4 54.5-55.0 °C). Elem. anal.: For C14H14O (198.27)
calc. (%): C, 84.81; H, 7.12; O, 8.07; found (%): C, 84.79; H, 7.08. 1H
NMR (ref.5) (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.41-7.37 (m, 2H), 7.31-7.36 (m, 2H), 7.26
(d, J = 13.6 Hz, 2H), 7.25 (m, 1H), 7.15 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 5.82 (s,
1H), 2.34 (s, 3H), 2.19 (brs, 1H). 13C NMR (ref.5) (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ
144.28, 141.29, 137.63, 129.52, 128.79, 127.79, 126.86, 126.78, 76.44,
21.45.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Nozaki-Hiyama-Kishi reaction, alternative preparation shown
