$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of the previously synthesized aldehyde (1.2 g, 4.92 mmol, 1
equiv) in a 5/1 mixture of an aqueous solution of NH4Cl and THF (50 mL)
were added, at rt, prenyl bromide (954 mg, 6.40 mmol, 1.3 equiv) and zinc
(416 mg, 6.40 mmol, 1.3 equiv). After 4 h at rt, aq. NH4Cl (20 mL) and
EtOAc (20 mL) were added. The phases were separated and the aqueous layer
was extracted twice with EtOAc. The combined organic layers were washed
with brine, dried over MgSO4 and evaporated under reduced pressure.
Purification by flash chromatography (SiO2, PE/Et2O 100/0 to 98/2)
afforded the compound. Compound 6, Yield: (1.35 g, 88%), colorless oil.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
