$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM THF was degassed by freeze-thawing. To a stirred solution of aldehyde
10ad (175 mg, 0.189 mmol) in THF (4.0 mL) were added CHI3 (149 mg, 0.377
mmol) and CrCl2 (232 mg, 1.89 mmol) at room temperature in a glove box.
The mixture was stirred at room temperature for 6 h in a glove box and
filtered through a pad of florisil, and the residue was washed with
hexane-EtOAc (7:3). The filtrate and the washings were combined and
concentrated in vacuo. The crude product was purified by column
chromatography on silica gel (5.0 g, exane-EtOAc 9:1→17:3). Compound:
iodoolefin 11, Yield: 171 mg, 86% as a colorless oil. [α]28D +3.2 (c
1.73, CHCl3); IR (CHCl3) 3028, 2932, 1724, 1595, 1517, 1491, 1373, 1254,
1030, 837 cm-1; 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.46-7.41 (m, 6H), 7.32-7.27
(m, 6H), 7.25-7.21 (m, 3H), 6.91-6.86 (m, 2H), 6.82 (d, J= 8.0 Hz, 1H),
6.54 (ddd, J= 14.6, 8.1, 7.1 Hz, 1H), 6.04 (d, J= 14.6 Hz, 1H), 4.98 (dd,
J= 9.7, 2.4 Hz, 1H), 4.77 (d, J= 7.0 Hz, 1H), 4.69 (d, J= 7.0 Hz, 1H),
4.63 (d, J= 11.6 Hz, 1H), 4.48 (d, J= 11.6 Hz, 1H), 3.88 (s, 3H), 3.86
(s, 3H), 3.85 (m, 1H), 3.42 (m, 1H), 3.28 (s, 3H), 3.22 (ddd, J= 9.2,
7.0, 4.3 Hz, 1H), 3.11 (dt, J= 8.4, 3.8 Hz, 1H), 3.00 (dt, J= 9.2, 6.0
Hz, 1H), 2.28 (m, 1H), 2.18 (dt, J= 14.2, 7.1 Hz, 1H), 2.02 (m, 1H), 2.01
(s, 3H), 1.88 (m, 1H), 1.77-1.55 (m, 5H), 1.51 (ddd, J = 14.2, 7.1, 3.8
Hz, 1H), 1.46 (m, 1H), 1.36-1.17 (m, 2H), 0.94 (d, J= 7.0 Hz, 3H), 0.88
(s, 9H), 0.86 (d, J= 6.8 Hz, 3H), 0.71 (d, J= 6.8 Hz, 3H), 0.05 (s, 3H),
0.04 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (150 MHz, CDCl3) δ 170.8, 148.9, 148.5, 144.3 (3C),
143.4, 130.7, 128.6 (6C), 127.7 (6C), 126.9 (3C), 120.4, 111.2, 110.8,
95.3, 86.5, 81.7, 78.9, 78.6, 76.6, 69.5, 68.8, 61.3, 56.9, 55.9, 55.8,
43.3, 37.3, 36.7, 34.8, 31.0, 30.6, 29.5, 27.6, 25.8 (3C), 21.1, 18.0,
16.9, 15.0, 9.7, -4.5, -4.5; HRMS (ESI) m/z 1073.4439, calcd for
C56H79INaO9Si [M+Na]+1073.4436.
