$DATUM 8-(tert-Butyldimethylsilanyloxy)-3S,5S-dimethyloct-1-yn-4R-ol (17).
Triphenyl phosphine (89 mg, 0.34 mmol) was added to a stirring solution
of palladium(II) acetate (77 mg, 0.34 mmol) in anhydrous THF (60 mL) at
-78 °C. Stirring continued until a homogeneous solution was formed.
Aldehyde 16 (1.56 g, 6.80 mmol) and (R)-2-mesyloxy-3-butyne (1.50 g,
10.20 mmol) were added successively, followed by the dropwise addition of
Et2Zn (20.40 mL, 1 M solution in THF). The resulting yellow solution was
stirred at -78 °C for 15 min, then warmed to -20 °C and stirred for 36 h.
After quenching with saturated NH4Cl (50 mL) at -20 °C, the mixture was
extracted with ether (3 × 50 mL), the organic layers combined and dried
over Na2SO4. Purification by flash chromatography (SiO2, 10:1
hexanes/EtOAc) gave alcohol 17 (1.58 g, 82%) as a colorless oil. [α]25 D
-11.6 (c 1.12, CHCl3); 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 3.61 (t, J = 6.3 Hz,
2H), 3.25 (q, J = 5.8 Hz, 1H), 2.72-2.67 (m, 1H), 2.13 (d, J = 2.1 Hz,
1H), 1.80 (d, J = 6.6 Hz, 1H), 1.70-1.44 (m, 3H), 1.32-1.25 (m, 1H), 1.22
(d, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H), 0.95 (d, J = 6.6 Hz, 3H), 0.90 (s, 9H), 0.06 (s, 6H)
ppm; 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 85.7, 77.5, 70.9, 63.4, 35.8, 30.6, 30.3,
29.8, 26.0, 18.4, 17.8, 13.8, -5.3, -5.3 ppm; IR (film) 3439, 1643, 745
cm-1; HRMS (ESI) calcd for C15H29O2Si [M - CH3]+ 269.1937, found
269.1936.
