$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Nozaki-Hiyama-Kishi Reaction, Typical Experiment The solution of halogen
derivative (0.15mmol), aldehyde (0.2mmol), and NiCl2 (1mg) in 1mL DMA-THF
10:1 was degassed and treated with the eluate (2.7mL) obtained as
described previously (row 4, Table 1). Progress of the reaction was
monitored with gas chromatography-mass spectrometry (GC-MS) or ultra
performance liquid chromatography-mass spectrometry (UPLC-MS). After
stirring at 50°C for the time given in Table 2, the green reaction
mixture was diluted with water (20mL) and allowed to crystallize at rt
(compounds 2a-2g), or extracted with ether (3×50mL); the organic layer
washed with brine (6×20mL) and dried with magnesium sulfate. The
crystalline material resulting after evaporation was recrystallized from
ethanol (compounds 1a, 1b). The isolated yields and CrCl2 amounts are
given in Table 2. Diphenylmethanol (1a) The title compound was made from
iodobenzene (30.6 mg) and benzaldehyde (21.2 mg). White solid, 22.2 mg.
M.p. 68.1-68.5 °C (ref.2 68.0-68.5 °C). Elem. anal.: For C13H12O (184.24)
calc. (%): C, 84.75; H, 6.57; O, 8.68; found (%): C, 84.75; H, 6.53. 1H
NMR (ref.3) (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.40-7.32 (m, 8H), 7.27 (m, 2H), 5.85 (s,
1H), 2.24 (brs, 1H). 13C NMR (ref.3) (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ 144.13, 128.84,
127.92, 126.88, 76.60.
