$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of methyl (3S,
4E)-5-iodo-3-(triisopropylsilyloxy)-pent-4-enoate 23 Chromium(II)
chloride (1.40 g, 11.4 mmol) was flamedried under nitrogen, cooled to
room temperature and then THF (2.2 ml) was addedat 0 °C. A solution of
aldehyde 22a (0.375 g, 1.29 mmol) and iodoform (1.517 g, 3.85 mmol) in
dioxane (22 ml) was added to the chromium(II) chloride slurry viacannula
and the reaction heated to 40 °C for 16 h. Water (30 ml) was added at
room temperature and the reaction mixture extracted into Et2O (5 × 45
ml). The combined organic layers were washed with 10% sodium thiosulfate
solution, dried over MgSO4 and concentrated in vacuo. The residue was
purified by flash column chromatography, eluting with petrol to remove
the iodoform, followed by EtOAc to give vinyl iodide 23. Yellow oil,
yield 0.3495 g, 65%. [α]D 5. 23 -5.7 (c 1.39 in CHCl3); νmax/cm-1 2970
(CH), 2946 (CH), 2868 (CH), 1739 (C=O), 1366 (C-O), 1217 (C-O) and 1100
(Si-O); δH (270 MHz; CDCl3) 1.04 (21H, s, OTIPS), 2.49 (1H, dd, J 15 and
7, 2-HH), 2.61 (1H, dd, J 15 and 7, 2-HH), 3.67 (3H, s, OCH3), 4.67 (1H,
app qd, J 7 and 1, 3-H), 6.37 (1H, dd, J 14.5 and 1, 5-H), 6.61 (1H, dd,
J14.5 and 7, 4-H); δC (100 MHz; CDCl3) 16.8 (3×SiC(CH3)2), 22.5
(3×SiC(CH3)2), 47.6 (C-2), 56.3 (OCH3), 72.4 (C-3), 77.0 (C-5), 152.4
(C-4) and 175.4 (C-1); m/z (ESI+ ) 435 [M + Na]+ (35%), 413 (13%), 325
(12%), 302 (16%), 203 (6%); HRMS (ESI+ ) calculated for C15H29O3NaSiI
435.3720, found 435.0823.
